        'Icon and control legend' => [
            'body' => '<p>The same controls mean the same thing on every screen. This is the complete legend.</p><h4>Row actions</h4><ul><li><b>Green eye</b>. View the record without changing it.</li><li><b>Gold pencil</b>. Edit the record. On some list pages it opens the detail page already in edit mode.</li><li><b>Red bin</b>. Delete the record. A confirmation modal always appears first and names what is being deleted.</li><li><b>Grey icon</b>. A neutral action such as archive or download, which changes nothing about the figures.</li><li><b>Amber chip</b>. A state change that needs deliberate intent, for example <b>Close</b> on a financial period.</li></ul><h4>Model and calculation controls</h4><ul><li><b>Lock</b>. Freezes a result so it cannot be edited, for audit integrity. A locked matrix, loss given default run or effective interest rate is final; create a new draft rather than editing it.</li><li><b>Recalculate</b>. Runs a draft again with the current inputs. Not available once locked.</li><li><b>Apply</b> or <b>Book</b>. Writes a model result onto the loan book, for example applying a transition matrix so its probabilities become the loans\' probability of default.</li><li><b>Configuration cog</b>. Opens the settings behind a transition profile.</li><li><b>Reorder handle</b>. Drag to change the order of grading categories.</li></ul><h4>Filters and period controls</h4><ul><li><b>Calendar icon</b>. Marks every reporting period selector, so month-end pickers are easy to spot.</li><li><b>Layers icon</b>. Marks the portfolio filter.</li><li><b>Compare To</b>. On the dashboard, the earlier period every change chip is measured against.</li><li><b>Show filters</b> and <b>Hide filters</b>. Collapse or expand a filter panel. Filters persist in the page address, so a filtered view can be shared as a link.</li></ul><h4>Reading results</h4><ul><li><b>KPI tile</b>. A white card with a coloured left edge: green for exposure and volume, red for loss, amber for coverage and warnings.</li><li><b>Change chip</b>. The small arrow and percentage beside a figure. It is coloured by business meaning, not by direction: exposure rising is growth and reads green, while ECL, probability or loss rate rising is risk and reads red.</li><li><b>Badge colours</b>. Green means good or approved, gold or amber means pending or watch, red means adverse or blocked, grey means neutral or not applicable. Stage badges follow the same rule: Stage 1 green, Stage 2 amber, Stage 3 red.</li><li><b>Chart and table toggle</b>. Switches a visual between the chart and the underlying numbers.</li><li><b>Numbers</b>. Money is shown with thousands separators and two decimals, negatives in parentheses, right aligned. Probabilities and loss rates are shown as percentages.</li><li><b>Empty state</b>. Reads <b>No data available for this section.</b> rather than showing zeros, so a missing input is never mistaken for a real nil.</li></ul><h4>Shell controls</h4><ul><li><b>Bell</b>. Notifications, with a count badge when unread ones exist.</li><li><b>Avatar</b>. Your profile, password, two-factor authentication and sign out.</li><li><b>Help button</b>. Opens the manual article written for the page you are on, where one is mapped.</li><li><b>Loading pill</b>. A gold <b>Loading</b> pill while a page is fetching, and a green <b>Done</b> flash when it arrives.</li><li><b>Export buttons</b>. <b>CSV</b> for the raw rows, <b>Download PDF</b> for the branded document, <b>Excel</b> for a branded workbook with typed numbers.</li></ul>',
